		{
			"id": "Decisions",
			"route": "/decisions",
			"type": "index",
			"title": "Decisions",
			"config": {
				"register": "decidesk",
				"schema": "decision",
				"quickFilters": [
					{
						"label": "Decisions",
						"filter": {},
						"default": true
					},
					{
						"label": "Motions",
						"icon": "icon-comment",
						"filter": {
							"decisionType": "motion"
						},
						"page": "Motions",
						"route": "Motions"
					}
				],
				"_motionsFilterNote": "REQ-RMN-003 — Motions is one decisionType of the unified Decision supertype (ADR-005), not a sibling concept. This quick-filter surfaces Motions AS a filtered view of Decisions (decisionType=motion, a STORED/queryable field merged server-side into the OpenRegister fetch — no client-side derivation, unlike effectiveStatus per the _inForceFilterNote). The retained Motions index page (pages[] id `Motions`, route /motions) carries the same filter plus motion-specific columns/tabs; the `page`/`route` hints let the strip deep-link there. The standalone top-level Motions menu leaf was retired (REQ-RMN-001) so Motions is reachable through its parent Decisions surface rather than as a peer top-level item.",
				"columns": [
					{
						"key": "title",
						"label": "Title",
						"widget": "link"
					},
					{
						"key": "lifecycle",
						"label": "Lifecycle",
						"widget": "badge"
					},
					{
						"key": "outcome",
						"label": "Outcome",
						"widget": "badge"
					},
					{
						"key": "decisionDate",
						"label": "Decision date",
						"formatter": "date"
					},
					{
						"key": "isPublished",
						"label": "Publication",
						"widget": "badge"
					},
					{
						"key": "effectiveStatus",
						"label": "Effective status",
						"widget": "badge",
						"computed": true
					},
					{
						"key": "legalBasis",
						"label": "Legal basis",
						"hidden": true
					}
				],
				"_inForceFilterNote": "DESIGN D3 — the in-force filter operates over the derived effectiveStatus, which (per design D2) is NOT a stored/queryable field: OpenRegister cannot express the inbound supersedes/repeals lookup as a materialised calculation, so effectiveStatus is computed client-side. A static manifest `filter` (the proven Motions decisionType pattern) and `quickFilters` both merge a filter map into the OpenRegister fetch and therefore only work over STORED fields — neither can server-filter on a client-derived value. The in-force / superseded / repealed state is instead surfaced per-decision via the effectiveStatus badge column (computed client-side) plus the banner and incoming-relation groups in RelatedDecisionsTab. A server-side in-force filter becomes available only if/when effectiveStatus is materialised by an OpenRegister inverse-relation calculation operator (D2 follow-up).",
				"actions": [
					{
						"id": "view",
						"label": "View",
						"icon": "icon-toggle",
						"handler": "navigate",
						"route": "DecisionDetail",
						"primary": true
					},
